      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-taeniata-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Listed in the IBC as part of the Betta picta complex. IUCN Red List: Unknown. The body is grayish brown with blue iridescence on the fins. The male also has iridescent blue cheeks.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-taeniata-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Found in Kalimantan.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-taeniata-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Still pools and small streams.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-taeniata-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>A pair per 19 litres (5 gallons) is recommended.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-taeniata-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<ul><li>TDS: 60–200 (kept in soft water with low TDS, but tolerant of a variety of water conditions)</li><li>pH: 5.0–7.0</li><li>Temperature: 24–29°C (75–85°F); much better coloration at warmer temperatures above 26°C (78°F)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-taeniata-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Fed live blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-taeniata-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Fairly peaceful and can be kept in groups. Males show off and flare at each other from time to time, but no real harm is done.</p>"
    },
